ARES-X – Interactive Mars Surface Simulation

Main Product

The Interactive Mars Surface Simulation is the central product of ARES-X. It helps users explore Martian terrain, examine scientific data and investigate potential astronaut exploration routes.

Demonstration Location

Jezero Crater, Mars.

Demonstration Sequence

1. Interactive Mars Explorer

- Open the interactive Mars model.
- Rotate, zoom and explore the Martian surface.
- Select Jezero Crater.

2. Scientific Data Layers

Demonstrate the six data categories presented in our project:

- Optical
- Thermal
- Spectral
- Topographic
- Radiation
- Geological

3. Terrain Analysis

- Explore elevation information.
- Examine terrain and slope.
- Identify potential surface hazards.

4. Route Planning

- Select a scientific exploration objective.
- Compare two hypothetical routes.
- Review terrain and potential exposure risks.

5. Supporting Systems

- Scientific Research
- Mission Dashboard
- MARIO AI Assistant
- Research Report Generator

Project Objective

Bring planetary exploration data into one interactive environment to support research, mission planning and astronaut safety.

Data Sources

- NASA / JPL Mars Trek
- USGS–NASA Planetary Geologic Mapping Program
- NASA Mars Perseverance Raw Images Gallery
- NASA Worldview

Scientific Integrity

Distinguish operational features from proposed features, illustrative graphics and simulations. Clearly identify the source and limitations of every dataset and calculation.

